## 📐 Network Architecture & Topology

### 1. Main Campus
Divided logically across three distinct facilities managed under a centralized distribution layer.

*   **Building A:**
    *   **Administration** (VLAN 10 | `192.168.1.0/24`)
    *   **Human Resources** (VLAN 20 | `192.168.2.0/24`)
    *   **Finance** (VLAN 30 | `192.168.3.0/24`)
    *   **Faculty of Business** (VLAN 40 | `192.168.4.0/24`)
*   **Building B:**
    *   **Faculty of Engineering & Computing** (VLAN 50 | `192.168.5.0/24`)
    *   **Faculty of Arts & Design** (VLAN 60 | `192.168.6.0/24`)
*   **Building C:**
    *   **Student Labs** (VLAN 70 | `192.168.7.0/24`)
    *   **IT Department** (VLAN 80 | `192.168.8.0/24`) *(Hosts internal university Web & FTP servers)*

### 2. Branch Campus (Faculty of Health & Sciences)
*   **Staff Department:** (VLAN 90 | `192.168.9.0/24`)
*   **Student Labs:** (VLAN 100 | `192.168.10.0/24`)

### 3. External Edge Cloud
*   **External Email Server Domain:** Hosted behind an isolated static cloud router (`20.0.0.0/30`).

